From caf6afee8730b1faa38c73e7e83f7513001970f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kunal Jha <kunal.jha3@in.ey.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 08:08:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(dev): a local full stack on an embedded PostgreSQL,
 loaded through the real loaders

FRONTEND_HARDENING.md section 1. `python scripts/dev_stack.py` starts a
self-contained PostgreSQL 16, applies all 17 migrations, loads the seed,
generates synthetic Form 20 / PS list / roll PDFs, loads them through the
documented loader CLIs with the AC-total reconciliation gate on, refreshes all
14 materialized views, creates one user per role, prints the credentials and
serves the API on :8000. No Docker, no service, no administrator rights.

This is the first time anything in this repository has run against a database.
DECISIONS.md D-002 recorded every gate that needed one as NOT VERIFIED HERE;
that constraint is gone, and twelve defects surfaced the moment it was.

Prerequisite (N4, D-005). PostGIS, pg_trgm and unaccent become optional: 0001
records what the cluster has in `schema_capability` and, without PostGIS,
defines the five ST_* functions this codebase calls over the built-in point and
polygon types; 0002 declares its two geometry columns accordingly. Application
SQL is identical either way. `vector` stays required.

Defects this found, all verified by command, none by reading:

- N9  `ingest/resolve.py` was never called. All six steps of master prompt 3.1
      were implemented and pinned by 70 tests while `parse_form20` still used
      the bracket-splitting lookup C1 describes. The fix for the audit's most
      consequential defect was written and not wired in.
- N10 parse_form20, parse_pslist, parse_roll and caste_estimate all inserted
      without `ac_id`, NOT NULL on sixteen tables since 0014. None of them
      could write a single row against the current schema.
- N14 0015_metrics.sql selected `l.ac_id` from a table with no such column, so
      the migration could not be applied at all.
- N13 passlib 1.7.4 with bcrypt 5.0.0 made every hash_password() call raise, so
      no user could be created and no password login could succeed (D-008).
- N7  NOTA never reached result_booth, so valid_votes excluded it and every
      share, margin and turnout figure used a denominator ~1% too small. D1 in
      a new place: resolve.py's NOTA branch is unreachable because NOTA is a
      tail column.
- N5  mv_result_booth_wide took electors from a column no loader writes, so
      turnout was NULL for every booth however many rolls were loaded.
- N8  the crosswalk leaked an orphan booth per unmatched station on every
      re-run, and the runbook tells operators to re-run.
- N11 parse_roll upserted on a constraint 0014 had dropped (B11, loader half).
- N12 parse_pslist built booth_uid from the PS number (B5, loader half).
- N6  the surname lookup read surname_hi only, so a Latin-script roll produced
      zero caste coverage and reported it as coverage, not as script.
- N16 tests/e2e/test_metrics_sql.py was not re-runnable: on its first real run
      one case passed and thirteen errored.
- N15 api/routers/data.py and booth_card.py read `votes_counted`, renamed
      `votes_polled` by 0015, so /acs/{ac}/summary 500s. Left open for
      section 2, whose route-by-role contract test should find the rest.

Closes H.1, H.3, H.4 and H.9, and B1 (parse_roll --link-election is the writer
election_roll_link never had). C5 and C15 closed; C7 and C8 now tested.

New: scripts/dev_stack.py, ingest/mock_documents.py, common/pdf_writer.py,
ingest/acscope.py, tests/e2e/test_ingest_pipeline.py.

Gates: pytest 756 passed, 1 skipped; tests/e2e 123 passed (was 0 runnable);
npm run build clean; scripts/lint_sql.py clean; no secret staged.
DECISIONS.md D-005 to D-008. NEXT_STEPS.md is left untracked - it is not mine.

